// @vibe/compiler/entry/compiler/fs_compile — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-
// internal contract, part of entry/'s own explicit "high risk" sub-batch
// (issue #897 body: "高リスク (要個別設計判断)... entry/ とそのサブディレ
// クトリ"), migrated alongside entry/compiler/, entry/source_compile/, and
// entry/source_compile/wasi_only/ in the same batch. Directory-shared-scope
// package (2 impl files, ~1080 lines): the multi-module / source-group
// compile drivers (prepare_modules_cached, compile_with_modules*,
// compile_with_closure_sources_*, compile_with_source_groups_*, the
// source_group_*_count selfbuild probes, fs_compile.vibe) plus the
// import-closure ordering + path-resolution helpers backing them
// (collect_inline_sources_ordered, source_lookup_*, closure_order.vibe).
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `entry`, dual-row: this contract + fs_compile.vibe;
// closure_order.vibe already had its own row and is unchanged).
//
// Naming: the old index.vibe was not a facade but real implementation (the
// directory's larger file, 823 lines), so it moved verbatim to
// fs_compile.vibe -- no collision (fs_compile/fs_compile.vibe did not
// exist), same convention as loader.vibe/runtime.vibe/core.vibe.
//
// Same-directory export-name collision (found only by reading both files'
// export lists side by side, not by any build failure -- check_contract's
// two-loop design tolerates two sibling files exporting the same name at
// the same signature without erroring, see contract/contract.vibe's
// check_contract, so this was silently latent): BOTH fs_compile.vibe and
// closure_order.vibe defined their own `export fn closure_ordered_source_count
// (main_source: String, main_path: String, sources: Array[(String, String)])
// -> Int with Exception` -- fs_compile.vibe's is a thin wrapper around the
// imported `collect_inline_sources_ordered`, closure_order.vibe's is the
// same computation inlined via its own private traversal helpers; both
// return identical results for identical inputs, so this was accidental
// duplication, not a real behavioral fork. Pre-migration this was harmless
// (fs_compile.vibe never imports closure_order.vibe's copy by that name, so
// each file's own local definition served its own callers -- entry/compiler
// /index.vibe's facade calls fs_compile.vibe's version, the standalone
// closure_order.vibe copy was only reachable via a direct leaf import from
// tests/fs_compile_path_test.vibe). A single flat contract can only declare
// a name once, so closure_order.vibe's copy is renamed
// `closure_ordered_source_count_for_test` (matching its own sibling
// `_for_test` helpers -- source_lookup_exists_for_test,
// resolve_relative_path_for_test, first_import_resolved_path_for_test, ...);
// tests/fs_compile_path_test.vibe (its only caller) is updated to the new
// name and to the package-form import. fs_compile.vibe's own
// closure_ordered_source_count is untouched and is what
// entry/compiler/index.vpkg (this package's own facade consumer) declares
// and re-exports.
//
// External-caller fixes (literal `entry/compiler/fs_compile/index.vibe` /
// `entry/compiler/fs_compile/closure_order.vibe` leaf-path references,
// now that leaf-file imports from outside the package are rejected by
// enforce_incoming_boundary_fs): tests/fs_compile_path_test.vibe (leaf
// import of closure_order.vibe -> package-form `../entry/compiler/fs_compile`,
// plus the rename above), tests/module_loader_collect_sources_test.vibe
// (the fs_compile-entry assertion now targets index.vpkg and expects both
// fs_compile.vibe and closure_order.vibe alongside it, mirroring the
// existing codegen/index.vpkg assertion in the same test),
// selfbuild_gate_block_a.vibe's `selfbuild_probe_lex_entry_compiler` /
// `selfbuild_probe_parse_entry_compiler` family reference
// entry/compiler/index.vibe, not this directory, and are fixed by
// entry/compiler/index.vpkg's own migration instead. No import cycle found:
// fs_compile.vibe's own dependencies (syntax/, codegen/, codegen/wasi,
// checker/, core/, loader/, runtime/, cache/ (#897: now its own contract
// package too -- fs_compile.vibe imports it as `../../../cache { .. }`,
// not the old `cache/persistent_cache.vibe` leaf spelling), and
// module_graph_path.vibe (still a plain leaf file, pending a sibling
// relocation batch) -- don't import back into
// entry/compiler/fs_compile/; loader/index.vpkg's and runtime/index.vpkg's
// own header notes already record this directory as one of their fixed
// external callers (leaf `runtime/typecheck_fs.vibe` /
// `loader/manifest_sources.vibe` style references), confirming no reverse
// edge exists.
//
// No exported types: TypeDb (../../../runtime) arrives as structural
// signature text resolved against runtime/index.vpkg's own opaque
// declaration (loader/runtime precedent -- no re-import needed here).

